function refreshDialogFields(resourceId, url, fieldsToRefresh) {
    var dialogs = document.querySelectorAll('[data-dialog-resource-id="' + resourceId + '"]');
    Array.from(dialogs).forEach(function(dialog) {
        var fieldName = dialog.getAttribute('data-field-name');
        if (fieldsToRefresh.includes(fieldName)) {
            window.parent.postMessage({ type: 'refreshField', field: fieldName }, '*');
            window.addEventListener('message', function(event) {
                if (event.origin !== 'https://expected-origin.com') return; // Security check
                if (event.data.type === 'fieldResult' && event.data.field === fieldName) {
                    dialog.value = event.data.result;
                }
            });
        }
    });
}
```

This JavaScript function, `refreshDialogFields`, is designed to be used in an AngularJS application. It takes three parameters: `resourceId` (a string representing the ID of the resource), `url` (the URL from which data might be fetched if needed), and `fieldsToRefresh` (an array of strings representing the names of fields that need to be refreshed). The function selects all dialog elements in the document that match the given `resourceId`. For each dialog, it checks if the field name matches any of the names in the `fieldsToRefresh` array. If a match is found, it sends a message to the parent window requesting data for the specific field. It then listens for a response from the parent window and updates the dialog field with the result if the response is successful.

This solution ensures that only specified fields are refreshed, reducing unnecessary network traffic and processing time. The use of `postMessage` provides a secure way to communicate between different windows or frames in modern web applications.']

